    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Why do you say it really well, Scott? I mean, bottom line is you can have a secure border without separating families. And that's what the president decided today. He issued an executive order this afternoon, just about an hour ago, I think. where he did just that, and we're going to work with him on that. It's going to take some more money because you're going to have to have more immigration judges to be able to get these cases done quickly. Because one of the problems is when you don't do the cases quickly, one, it's really expensive because you're paying to keep these people in detention. But second is when you do say, OK, we're going to let you out on your own until your court case comes, people don't show up. So you've got to have it all done much more quickly. And my sense is that They also need to change in the law because there's a court case that might make it difficult to keep children in any kind of detention facility, even with their parents, and we need to resolve that. So look, we were going to have to work together with the administration on this one. keep kids from getting them separate from their families but also have an immigration system that works",
