    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, we got it through the House last week. We got it through the Senate Committee this week. The stop act basically says, let's stop the fentanyl, which is this terrible opioid, it's a synthetic opioid. from coming into our country from overseas. That's mostly coming in by mail. That's why it stops the post office from just allowing it to come in without screening. But then you've got some of it is coming in overland from Mexico, but you have crystal meth now coming in from Mexico coming northwest Ohio. And you obviously have heroin coming in from Mexico. So you've got to tighten up all of it. And that's not going to be the ultimate solution because as long as there's a strong demand, this poison will come in in some way. There's so much money in it. But you got to do both. You got to cut back on the supply. That will raise the cost. That will help on reducing the demand. And then you got to do better in terms of the prevention, the education, and obviously the treatment for people who are already because it is a disease and you got to deal with it that way",
